From 6cea497c13fa51f2794226385bd813e39bd4fc18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:17:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 106/110] MAS local: screenshot and volume buttons on the lean
 title bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The lean window's title bar had only back, home and the window buttons,
so a screenshot meant the full toolbar or Ctrl+S, and an instance that
plays sound had nothing to turn it down with. It now has, left of back:

- 截图 (ModAVD#231): the side toolbar's screenshot, TAKE_SCREENSHOT,
  saved where -save-path says (the manager passes Pictures\ModAVD;
  the folder is made when it is not there yet) with the flash. When it
  is not saved the lean window no longer opens an English dialog: a
  short note, 截图没存上, shows under the button (or in the message
  overlay without the title bar) and goes away by itself. The full
  toolbar (ANDROID_EMU_FULL_TOOLBAR=1) keeps its dialog. Off Windows the
  lean side toolbar keeps its screenshot button.

- 音量 (ModAVD#226), only while the emulator plays sound: the manager
  passes -audio none (and -feature -VirtioSndCard) when the instance's
  sound is off, and -no-audio / -noaudio hide it too. As MuMu has it, a
  click opens a bar under the button: a speaker on the left mutes and
  unmutes, a slider on the right sets the volume as it moves. A click
  anywhere outside the bar, the volume button included, closes it.

The bar sets Android's media volume (STREAM_MUSIC), not the host's
output gain: on opening it reads `cmd media_session volume --stream 3
--get` ("volume is 5 in range [0..15]"), so a change made in a game or
in Android's settings shows the next time, and the slider sends
`--set N`. Muting sets the minimum and unmuting the last index above
it (or half way up), since setting a stream's volume above zero unmutes
it and Android keeps the index across boots. adb goes through the
window's AdbInterface: the adb process runs and its output is read on
the interface's own thread, the answer comes back to the UI thread, and
the slider runs one command at a time with only its newest value
waiting, so a drag does not start an adb process per pixel. The adb
inherits the emulator's ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT, the manager's own
server; without it, with it set to 5037, or without an adb (the SDK's
platform-tools first), the button is disabled and its tool tip says
so, and nothing reaches adb's default server.

The icons are the dark theme's screen_shot and volume_up, drawn at the
window buttons' size, and a muted speaker in the same style.

The arithmetic is in lean-title-bar-logic, tested in
aemu-ui-lean-window_unittests (12 new tests): the buttons' order with and
without volume, when volume is shown, which ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT
values may be used, where the bar opens on the screen, the adb
arguments, parsing the volume line, the unmute index and the one at a
time sender. Mutation check: 15 of 15 mutants killed.

Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#231
Refs ModAVD/ModAVD#226

